{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ3D4jyfNAxumCjn5pdA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't get Netflix's total projected material cash requirements for 2025 with these tools. The total is in the \"Material Cash Requirements\" table of Netflix's FY2024 10-K, in the \"Next 12 Months\" column. A search confirmed that filing contains the table, but the search returns only a link, not the text. The total isn't published as structured XBRL data either, so I can't report it or rebuild it.\n\n**What I did find (FY2024 10-K, as of 31 December 2024):**\n- **Content obligations due in the next 12 months: $11,424,696,000 (about $11.42 billion).** This is only one part of the total. As a check, the same item was $10,328,923,000 a year earlier.\n\n**What's missing:**\n- **Debt principal and interest due in the next 12 months:** Netflix last published its one-year debt maturity as structured data in its FY2019 10-K, so there is no 2025 figure.\n- **Lease payments due in the next 12 months:** no structured data exists for this.\n- **The table's total:** without the parts above, I can't add up to it.\n\nThe full total is in the \"Material Cash Requirements\" section of the 10-K at the link below. The data also includes a later 10-K filed 23 January 2026, after your 16 May 2025 cutoff, so I left it out.\n\n**Sources**\n- Netflix Form 10-K for FY2024, filed 2025-01-27, accession 0001065280-25-000044 (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1065280/000106528025000044/nflx-20241231.htm)\n- Netflix Form 10-K for FY2023, filed 2024-01-26, accession 0001065280-24-000030 (prior-year comparison only)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1275,"cache_read_input_tokens":8965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1275},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"